Bubblegum — a Yapfast theme

The theme itself (theme.json, the pictures in art/ and previews/, and the
sounds in sounds/) is dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
The art (plastic texture, console body, LCD grid and bezel, D-pad and candy
face-button deck, composer keys, speaker grilles, power LED, holo sheen and
sticker, hover-bar stripes, dialog frame, pixel sparkles and heart) was generated procedurally for this theme; the sounds were
synthesised for it from square, triangle and noise waves. Neither uses any
outside source.

ICONS (icons/)

The pixel icons are Bubblegum's 16x16 redrawings of Yapfast's stock icons:
some drawn by hand on the pixel grid, the rest sampled from the stock shapes.
They are adaptations, so they keep the stock icons' licences:

- Icons based on Solar by 480 Design
  (https://www.figma.com/community/file/1166831539721848736), used under
  CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Changes: redrawn
  on a 16-pixel grid at a single solid weight.
- Icons based on Lucide (https://lucide.dev/): calendar, check, chevron-down,
  chevron-left, chevron-right, maximize, minimize, minus, restore, slash,
  square, x, forward and reply. ISC licence:
  Copyright (c) for portions of Lucide are held by Cole Bemis 2013-2022 as
  part of Feather (MIT). All other copyright (c) for Lucide are held by
  Lucide Contributors 2022.
  Permission to use, copy, modify, and/or distribute this software for any
  purpose with or without fee is hereby granted, provided that the above
  copyright notice and this permission notice appear in all copies.
  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND THE AUTHOR DISCLAIMS ALL WARRANTIES.
- The pixel versions of Yapfast's own icons (the logo, gif, hash, mic,
  signal, soundboard, thread, user and volume glyphs and the others the stock
  README lists as drawn for Yapfast) follow Yapfast's licence for them.

FONTS (fonts/)

Four font families, each under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1
(https://openfontlicense.org). Their full licence texts are in fonts/:

- fonts/Fredoka.ttf — Fredoka (variable, wdth 75–125, wght 300–700)
  Copyright 2016 The Fredoka Project Authors (https://github.com/hafontia/Fredoka-One)
  Licence: fonts/OFL-Fredoka.txt

- fonts/Silkscreen-Regular.ttf, fonts/Silkscreen-Bold.ttf — Silkscreen
  Copyright 2001 The Silkscreen Project Authors (https://github.com/googlefonts/silkscreen)
  Licence: fonts/OFL-Silkscreen.txt

- fonts/PixelifySans.ttf — Pixelify Sans (variable, wght 400–700)
  Copyright 2021 The Pixelify Sans Project Authors (https://github.com/eifetx/Pixelify-Sans)
  Licence: fonts/OFL-PixelifySans.txt

- fonts/DepartureMono.otf — Departure Mono 1.500
  Copyright 2022–2024 Helena Zhang (helenazhang.com)
  Licence: fonts/OFL-DepartureMono.txt

The fonts are unmodified and are not sold on their own.
